to-be-incorporated-into-paper-134 = referring (cons "**Arrays, and stuck primitive operations.** `Array n` is `Bytes (times n 8)` (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.10 “C20–C22 — Memory and state”, its part C22;" (cons "`lib/prim.cub`): `index n a i h` and `update n a i h v` with `h : le (suc i) n` are a load and a" (cons "store at offset `times i 8` with the proof that the access fits, `tabulate n f` writes `f` at" (cons "every index, and `index-update` (a read after a write at the same index is the value written)" (cons "is the byte layer's law `load64-store64` (trusted) unfolded. A primitive operation on a" (cons "variable is a neutral the checker views (`wprim k args`) and compares argument by argument, so" (cons "such laws follow by unfolding (an operation stuck on a variable used to be an unknown value). A law" (cons "stated as a primitive has no computation (`primitive name : T`): it is a constant of its type, and" (cons "a path among such constants reads its endpoints from that type, as any neutral path does." (cons "`Fin→Array n : Equiv (Fin n → Int64) (Array n)` is the interface (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.10 “C20–C22 — Memory and state”, its part C22, and §12 “The build list”, “C. Memory and state”, item 22): a program written" (cons "against functions uses application and `fin-set n f p v`, and under `atab` they are `index` and" (cons "`update` (`apply-by`, `fin-set-by`). Byte strings convert by their contents (`%beq`)." (cons "Other element types: `UInt32` on the 4-byte layer (`Array32`, `index32`/`update32`, `Fin→Array32`," (cons "its two laws trusted like the 8-byte ones), and any `A` with an equivalence to `Int64` on the 8-byte" (cons "layer (`indexV`/`updateV`/`Fin→ArrayV A to from ft tf n`): `Float64` by its bits (`f64bits`," (cons "`f64ofbits`, trusted inverse); the same on the 4-byte layer for any `A ≃ UInt32` (`Fin→ArrayV32`): `Float32` by its bits" (cons "(`f32bits`, `f32ofbits`; `Fin→ArrayF32`)." (cons "" nil)))))))))))))))))) (cons "In hyperactivity's language as the repository implements it: **Arrays, and stuck primitive operations.** `Array n` is `Bytes (times n 8)` (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.10 “C20–C22 — Memory and state”, its part C22;" (cons "`lib/prim.cub`): `index n a i h` and `update n a i h v` with `h : le (suc i) n` are a load and a" (cons "store at offset `times i 8` with the proof that the access fits, `tabulate n f` writes `f` at" (cons "every index, and `index-update` (a read after a write at the same index is the value written)" (cons "is the byte layer's law `load64-store64` (trusted) unfolded. A primitive operation on a" (cons "variable is a neutral the checker views (`wprim k args`) and compares argument by argument, so" (cons "such laws follow by unfolding (an operation stuck on a variable used to be an unknown value). A law" (cons "stated as a primitive has no computation (`primitive name : T`): it is a constant of its type, and" (cons "a path among such constants reads its endpoints from that type, as any neutral path does." (cons "`Fin→Array n : Equiv (Fin n → Int64) (Array n)` is the interface (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.10 “C20–C22 — Memory and state”, its part C22, and §12 “The build list”, “C. Memory and state”, item 22): a program written" (cons "against functions uses application and `fin-set n f p v`, and under `atab` they are `index` and" (cons "`update` (`apply-by`, `fin-set-by`). Byte strings convert by their contents (`%beq`)." (cons "Other element types: `UInt32` on the 4-byte layer (`Array32`, `index32`/`update32`, `Fin→Array32`," (cons "its two laws trusted like the 8-byte ones), and any `A` with an equivalence to `Int64` on the 8-byte" (cons "layer (`indexV`/`updateV`/`Fin→ArrayV A to from ft tf n`): `Float64` by its bits (`f64bits`," (cons "`f64ofbits`, trusted inverse); the same on the 4-byte layer for any `A ≃ UInt32` (`Fin→ArrayV32`): `Float32` by its bits" (cons "(`f32bits`, `f32ofbits`; `Fin→ArrayF32`)." nil)))))))))))))))))
